Best Winter Boots for Women of 2026

The Top Women’s Winter Boots for Warmth, Waterproofness, Fit, Comfort, and Ice Traction

October 5th, 2026 with a new winner for best winter hiking boot, best insulated winter boot, best pull-on, best for walking, and most comfortable winter bootHome > Gear Reviews > Footwear

Winter boots have a big job. They need to keep your feet warm and dry through snow, slush, ice, and cold without being so bulky or uncomfortable that you don’t want to wear them. I’ve spent winters in Alaska, Maine, New Hampshire, New York, and Colorado, and I’ve learned that the right winter boot depends as much on what you’re doing as how cold it is outside.

We’ve tested women’s winter boots in icy conditions, wet snow, deep snow, and extreme cold, using them for everything from hiking and snowshoeing to shoveling, walking the dog, running errands, and working outside. Some of these boots have stayed in our rotation for years, which has also given us a good sense of how they hold up over time.

We looked most closely at warmth, tread, waterproofness, fit, and shaft height. We also considered ankle and arch support, how well each boot worked with different socks, durability, and whether the boot made sense for its intended use.

Top Pick: The SOREL Joan of Arctic Boots are our favorite overall. We’ve worn them through winters from Maine to Alaska and keep coming back to their combination of warmth, waterproofness, traction, durability, and style. They’re sturdy enough for snow and outdoor chores but still easy to wear around town, and the replaceable liner helps extend the life of the boot.

Looking for men’s boots? See our Best Men’s Winter Boots guide.

Looking for kids’ boots? See our Best Kids’ Snow Boots guide.

We create reader-supported, objective gear reviews independently selected by our editors. This story may contain affiliate links, which help fund our website. When you click on the links to purchase gear, we may get a commission — without costing you an extra cent. Thank you for supporting our work and mission of outdoor coverage for every body! Learn more.

Women’s Winter Boots Comparison Table

