## Item text
Best Winter Gloves of 2026

Warm, thin, lightweight gloves for running, cycling, and extreme cold

A good pair of winter gloves can make all the difference for all-season running, cycling, hiking, and snowplay. Photo by Robert Curzon.

October 2nd, 2026, updated with two new winnersHome > Gear Reviews > Apparel

When cold weather gets serious, your hands often feel it first. I’ve spent winters in Alaska, Colorado, and Maine, and I’ve worn winter gloves while skiing, hiking, saddling horses in snowstorms, digging vehicles out of snowbanks, and chasing Alaskan huskies across frozen lakes. I love being outside in winter, but only if I can still feel my hands.

For this guide, we tested winter gloves for everything from everyday chores and dog walks to running, cycling, skiing, hiking, and long days outside in the cold. We used them in snowstorms, icy conditions, wet snow, and deep cold to see which ones stayed warm and comfortable without making it impossible to actually use our hands.

We paid closest attention to warmth, weather protection, comfort, durability, dexterity, and fit. Depending on the glove, we also tested touchscreen use, cycling grip, and heated settings, because what matters in a lightweight running glove is very different from what matters in a mitten made for extreme cold.

Top Pick: The North Face Denali Etip Gloves are our favorite overall because they hit a useful middle ground between warmth, dexterity, durability, and price. They’re warm enough for many everyday winter activities without feeling bulky, and we found them easy to use for the kinds of tasks where you still need your fingers to work.

If you’re looking for ski and snowboard-specific gloves, check out our Best Ski Gloves and Best Snowboard Gloves and Mittens guides

We create reader-supported, objective gear reviews independently selected by our editors. This story may contain affiliate links, which help fund our website. When you click on the links to purchase gear, we may get a commission — without costing you an extra cent. Thank you for supporting our work and mission of outdoor coverage for every body! Learn more.

Winter Gloves Comparison Table

*We note any discounts we see on our Deals page, which is updated daily.

For more of our most popular Winter Gear Guide stories:

